WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:14.353
Start and controls
Take a seat and press Ready. The host starts when everyone is ready. Your cards or dice are at the bottom.

00:00:14.353 --> 00:00:20.654
Follow the turn prompt. Wait for animations to finish; an expired turn is played automatically. Use Return to room after settlement.

00:00:20.654 --> 00:00:32.656
Reversi: start with four discs
We keep the dark player’s perspective throughout. Dark moves first on the 8×8 board, then light.

00:00:32.656 --> 00:00:46.657
Goal: finish with more discs
Bracket opposing discs to turn them into your colour. A lead in the middle of the match does not guarantee victory.

00:00:46.657 --> 00:00:57.657
Choose a legal empty square
Dots mark legal destinations on your turn. Click to play with a mouse; touch previews first, then use Confirm or tap the same square again.

00:00:57.657 --> 00:01:06.656
On touch, Cancel lets you choose again. One-tap mode skips confirmation.

00:01:06.656 --> 00:01:15.456
Every bracketed disc flips
The first move has flipped the white disc between the dark discs. Now watch light bracket a disc in reply.

00:01:15.456 --> 00:01:22.656
There must be at least one continuous opposing disc between the new disc and an existing friendly disc, with no empty gap.

00:01:22.656 --> 00:01:40.656
Check all eight directions
Horizontal, vertical and diagonal lines all count. A move can flip several directions at once. Follow the move list and last-move marker.

00:01:40.656 --> 00:01:56.657
Faster play: edges and corners
We speed up the next legal moves. A corner disc cannot be bracketed again; consider which replies your move leaves available.

00:01:56.657 --> 00:02:05.457
Rule card: automatic passes
Pause here to explain passing. There is no separate pass button to operate.

00:02:05.457 --> 00:02:12.656
A player with no legal square passes automatically. When neither player can move, the match ends even if squares remain empty.

00:02:12.656 --> 00:02:38.656
Fast-forward through the middle and endgame
Every remaining move is retained as the empty squares fill. Disc counts can swing repeatedly before the final count.

00:02:38.656 --> 00:02:50.659
The last empty square
One square remains. After this placement the server checks whether either player still has a legal move.

00:02:50.659 --> 00:02:58.359
Result: dark wins 44–20
After 60 placements, dark has 44 discs and light 20. Review the outcome, reason and move count, then use Back to room.

00:02:58.359 --> 00:03:05.667
Equal final disc counts draw. A draw offer on your turn also needs the opponent’s agreement.
